content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-107 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22950.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 5.5 mm/s RMS. Figure 3 is the applicable limit because it classifies HF-300 vibration velocity measured on bearing housings. The reading is in Zone C (4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS): 'Restricted - plan maintenance.' It is not in Zone D, whose label is 'Damage likely - stop the pump.' The manual requires weekly measurements on both bearing housings and classification of the highest reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Last month's vibration reading of 3.0 mm/s RMS was in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation,' under the same Figure 3 limits. The reported increase is 2.5 mm/s RMS and the classification has changed from Zone B to Zone C.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 76 C. The applicable limits are the HF-300 bearing-housing temperature limits, with temperature measured on the housing surface: normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. Therefore 76 C is 6 C above the normal limit but remains 4 C below alarm and 14 C below trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported. The troubleshooting action to replace the mechanical seal applies to the symptom 'leakage at shaft seal,' which is not reported here. The evidence provides no numerical allowable leakage-rate limit for any further comparison.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Check misalignment first: it is a documented cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, so it could explain both abnormal findings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check bearing wear next: it is also a documented cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature. Bearing condition and any noise must be established by inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a documented possible cause of the above-normal bearing temperature; check grease quantity rather than assuming bearing failure.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage is a documented possible cause of the high vibration and requires impeller inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation is another documented possible cause of high vibration; the manual directs the technician to check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Schedule planned maintenance for the Zone C condition. At the next route check, and before work-order close-out, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, record both results and classify the highest using Figure 3. Stop the pump if a reading falls in Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Diagnose before authorizing parts replacement: check shaft alignment, inspect the bearings and impeller, check NPSH and check grease quantity. Record evidence of misalignment, bearing wear or noise, impeller imbalance or damage, cavitation and over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing-replacement branch: if either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair—drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3). Do not replace only the drive-end bearing when the pair-replacement criterion applies.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket. Where back pull-out removal is required, the rotating assembly can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework; use the required lifting equipment identified in the safety controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal work is contingent on an actual repair need, not automatic from the no-leakage report. If seal replacement is required: isolate and drain the pump; remove the back pull-out assembly; remove the impeller nut and impeller; withdraw the seal and sleeve; and inspect the sleeve. For serial HF3-22950, do not fit HF3-450. Fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B and a new casing gasket. No sleeve measurement is needed to set HF3-450B, but replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For fasteners actually used in the reassembly, Table 5 values for lightly oiled threads are: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. Do not use Table 5's 25 Nm seal-gland value on this asset; HF3-450B seal gland nuts require 30 Nm under SB-2026-014.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. The applicable tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Conditional on the bearing-replacement inspection criterion; this is one of the two bearings that must be replaced as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Conditional on the bearing-replacement inspection criterion; replace together with HF3-512 when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Conditional on casing opening or execution of the documented seal-replacement procedure; replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal, conditional only if seal replacement is required. It is the mandatory substitute for HF3-450 on this serial and needs no sleeve measurement for seal setting; quantity is one for the single mechanical-seal position.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional on seal-disassembly inspection. Replace if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth under the bulletin applicable to serial HF3-22950.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "The supplied readings do not require an immediate manual stop: vibration is Zone C rather than Zone D, and temperature is below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. Continue to treat the pump as restricted and plan maintenance; stop it if vibration falls in Zone D, labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump.' Monitor housing-surface temperature against the documented alarm and trip limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any mechanical-seal replacement, isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly has a mass of 68 kg; lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge. Never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement: standard time is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians for replacement of the bearing pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time is 1.5 hours with 1 technician; it is required after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical-seal replacement: standard time is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. Do not add this allowance to the committed scope unless seal replacement is actually required.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection and gland torque conflict: manual Revision D lists component seal HF3-450, and Table 5 gives M10 seal gland nuts 25 Nm for lightly oiled threads. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits fitting HF3-450 and instead requires pre-set cartridge HF3-450B at 30 Nm on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-107 is serial HF3-22950, so the bulletin explicitly applies and controls any seal work on this asset. The manual's issue date is not supplied, so this decision rests on the bulletin's stated issue date and serial range, not an assumed publication sequence.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve acceptance differs in specificity: manual procedure 5.2 only says to inspect the sleeve for scoring, while the applicable bulletin requires replacement of HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Use the bulletin's 0.1 mm criterion for this serial. Its statement that no sleeve measurement is needed applies to setting the pre-set HF3-450B and does not eliminate the scoring inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration reading? The manual requires readings on both housings and classification of the highest, so the supplied drive-end reading alone cannot confirm completion of that check.",
    "What are the inspection results for alignment, grease quantity, bearing wear or noise, impeller condition and NPSH? These findings are needed to select the actual corrective repair and confirm which conditional parts and labour are required.",
    "What completion date should be assigned to the Zone C restricted/planned-maintenance condition? The evidence gives no maximum operating interval or scheduling deadline for Zone C.",
    "What labour allowance should be used for the initial diagnostic inspection and any post-maintenance route verification? Table 6 provides standard times only for seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment."
  ]
}
